cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If this software contributes to work you publish, please cite it. A citation is the
  thing that helps; co-authorship is not requested and could not be required — see the
  Citation section of README.md for why, and for the standing invitation to collaborate
  where a joint contribution is genuinely earned.
title: "dualis: physics for simulated worlds, checked against closed forms"
abstract: >-
  A Rust workspace of sixteen crates: a kernel that knows conservation, integration,
  scheduling and sampling but no physics, ten domain crates built on it, and scene and
  view layers above. Every claim is checked against a closed form, an exact limit, a
  conservation law or a convergence rate rather than against a second implementation.
  Results are bit-for-bit reproducible across platforms, optimisation levels,
  WebAssembly and thread counts, with a pinned digest that says so.
type: software
authors:
